Description:
    ShinyPopGen is an interactive Shiny application for population genetics
    analyses based on multilocus individual genotype datasets. It provides
    tools for data import and formatting, allele frequency and missing-data
    exploration, general statistics (Na, Ne, Ho, He), local and global
    panmixia (FIS, FIT), population subdivision (FST), and genetic
    diversities (HS, HT), all based on the Weir & Cockerham (1984)
    estimators. It also provides pairwise linkage disequilibrium testing,
    null allele frequency estimation with ENA correction (Chapuis & Estoup
    2007, FreeNA), and isolation-by-distance analysis with a Mantel test
    (Rousset 1997). Confidence intervals and significance are obtained by
    bootstrap resampling and Monte Carlo permutation, parallelised in C++
    via Rcpp and OpenMP.
